*  KW-3 witness (s147): the PRIMITIVE-PATTERN KEYWORD FAMILY must BEHAVE as its
*  pattern, not merely report DATATYPE=PATTERN.  Manual Ch.16 p.187-188 names each
*  a protected read-only repository of a fundamental system pattern: "&ARB The
*  primitive pattern ARB", and likewise BAL/REM/FAIL/FENCE/ABORT/SUCCEED.
*
*  PINS THE s147 REGRESSION: CN-2 re-keyed the tier-3 keyword read from the bare
*  name to a canonical "&Name", severing the bridge by which &ARB reached the bare
*  ARB pattern variable -- every one of these then fell into the user-constant tier
*  and raised error 342 ON READ.  kw_datatypes.sno caught the DATATYPE symptom;
*  nothing pinned the BEHAVIOUR.  This file does, so the class cannot go silent again.
*
*  SCOPE IS THE LANDED SN4-PAT SUBSET ON PURPOSE.  Only &ARB and &REM are used as
*  pattern OPERANDS here, because SCRIP's lowerer rejects &BAL/&FAIL/&FENCE/&SUCCEED/
*  &ABORT in a pattern outright ("pattern shape outside the SN4-PAT subset") -- a
*  SEPARATE, LARGER gap that is not this witness's business.  The remaining five are
*  therefore pinned at the READ, which is the exact operation the regression broke;
*  promote them to real matches when the pattern subset widens.
	&ANCHOR = 0
	S = 'abcdef'
	S ? &ARB . X 'cd'					:F(FARB)
	OUTPUT = 'ARB-match=' X
	S ? 'cd' &REM . Y					:F(FREM)
	OUTPUT = 'REM-match=' Y
	OUTPUT = 'BAL-read=' DATATYPE(&BAL)
	OUTPUT = 'FAIL-read=' DATATYPE(&FAIL)
	OUTPUT = 'FENCE-read=' DATATYPE(&FENCE)
	OUTPUT = 'ABORT-read=' DATATYPE(&ABORT)
	OUTPUT = 'SUCCEED-read=' DATATYPE(&SUCCEED)
	OUTPUT = 'PATTERN-KEYWORDS-OK'				:(END)
FARB	OUTPUT = 'FAIL: &ARB did not match'			:(END)
FREM	OUTPUT = 'FAIL: &REM did not match'			:(END)
END
